# Placeholder secrets for macro-inc/macro's local dev stack, for contributors
# without access to macro-inc's private Doppler `local` project (the normal
# source of these values). Doppler pull fails gracefully without them — see
# SKILL.md section 3 — these just fill the gap so services boot.
#
# Functionally broken with these placeholders: Google/GitHub/Slack OAuth,
# Stripe, LiveKit calls, GitHub App sync, Apollo/OpenAI/Cohere enrichment,
# email attachment CloudFront signing. The core app (frontend, auth session,
# docs, channels, tasks, local Postgres/Redis/Kafka/OpenSearch) all work.
#
# Three families of value in this file need runtime substitution — the skill
# script fills these in, they are NOT usable as committed static values:
#   1. MACRO_DB_URL / DATABASE_URL_READONLY — must match the real generated
#      Postgres credentials in infra/local/generated/<instance>/local.generated.env
#      (DATABASE_URL there), not a guessed postgres:postgres.
#   2. MACRO_API_TOKEN_PRIVATE_SECRET_KEY / MACRO_API_TOKEN_PUBLIC_KEY — must
#      be a real RSA keypair (RS256, parsed as PEM by jsonwebtoken), generated
#      fresh per bootstrap. A plain string boots the service but panics the
#      first time a token is actually signed/verified.
# Everything else below is a stable placeholder, safe to use as-is.

